{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522033-m20-phylactery","id":1522033,"title":"M20 Phylactery","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-09-03T22:24:18-07:00","id":1522033,"title":"M20 Phylactery","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> How does a Phylactery work with Correspondence? The rules as written make it impossible to use remotely, as per the Book of Secrets p. 95<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your mage must be <b>able to physically access</b> the phylactery in order<br /> to employ Sphere magick.\u200b </div> </div> </div>But latter says:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, you may use<br /> Correspondence Sphere magick to reach the phylactery,<br /> and you are always counted as being one success away<br /> from your phylactery when you use Correspondence to<br /> reach out to it.\u200b </div> </div> </div>Since you need to touch the phylactery to use Spheres how come you can remotely access it in the first place? Isnt this a contradiction? Access is a precondition to use magick.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, assuming that Correspondence somehow lets you use the Phylactery at distance, there is no longer need to use it blatantly to cast magick, right?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-04T00:29:05-07:00","id":1522038,"title":"","content":"\u201cIf the phylactery is taken from you, or you\u2019re taken away from it, you can retrieve it, or return to it, with a successful application of the Correspondence Sphere. The difficulty for this return Effect is 4 if the return would seem coincidental to a witness, 5 if it\u2019s vulgar without witnesses, and 6 if it\u2019s vulgar with witnesses. (Yes, the usual Paradox applies.)\u200b\u201c<br /> <br /> it specifically states in the flaw that one of the perks of a phylactery is that you can use corr magic to retrieve/return to it.<br /> <br /> This perk is not about using the phylactery at a distance, it\u2019s about getting your phylactery back to you such that you can do other magic once again.<br /> <br /> Setting up the gateway as mentioned in the paragraph you quote is something you need to do while with your phylactery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 09-04-2023, 03:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-05T12:35:58-07:00","id":1522114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522033-m20-phylactery?p=1522038#post1522038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cIf the phylactery is taken from you, or you\u2019re taken away from it, you can retrieve it, or return to it, with a successful application of the Correspondence Sphere. The difficulty for this return Effect is 4 if the return would seem coincidental to a witness, 5 if it\u2019s vulgar without witnesses, and 6 if it\u2019s vulgar with witnesses. (Yes, the usual Paradox applies.)\u200b\u201c<br /> <br /> it specifically states in the flaw that one of the perks of a phylactery is that you can use corr magic to retrieve/return to it.<br /> <br /> This perk is not about using the phylactery at a distance, it\u2019s about getting your phylactery back to you such that y<b>ou can do other magic once again.<br /> <br /> Setting up the gateway as mentioned in the paragraph you quote is something you need to do while with your phylactery.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry, I am not understanding.<br /> <br /> <br /> IF I have the Phylactery away from me, I can not use any Sphere, at all EXCEPT Correspondence to call it back to me? That is what you are saying?<br /> <br /> OR can I use Correspondence to count as touching it always and use it at distance? (until someone dispels the remote-touch effect)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-05T12:50:30-07:00","id":1522115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522033-m20-phylactery?p=1522114#post1522114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sorry, I am not understanding.<br /> <br /> <br /> IF I have the Phylactery away from me, I can not use any Sphere, at all EXCEPT Correspondence to call it back to me? That is what you are saying?<br /> <br /> OR can I use Correspondence to count as touching it always and use it at distance? (until someone dispels the remote-touch effect)</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the benefits that having a phylactery merit provides is that you may use correspondence to call your phylactery to you or yourself to your phylactery.<br /> <br /> this is the exception, all other sphere effects require you have physical contact with your phylactery","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-05T15:11:19-07:00","id":1522124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One of the benefits that having a phylactery merit </div> </div> </div>Phylactery is a Flaw.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-05T20:40:13-07:00","id":1522136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522033-m20-phylactery?p=1522115#post1522115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of the benefits that having a phylactery merit provides is that you may use correspondence to call your phylactery to you or yourself to your phylactery.<br /> <br /> <b>this is the exception, all other sphere effects require you have physical contact with your phylactery</b></div> </div> </div> </div>This is what confuses me, bolded my confusions:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Your mage must be able to physically access the phylactery in order<br /> to employ Sphere magick.</b> And therein lays the Flaw.\u200b<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <b>If the phylactery is taken from you, or you\u2019re taken away<br /> from it, you can retrieve it, or return to it, with a successful<br /> application of the Correspondence Sphere.\u200b</b><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <b>You cannot perform magick or recharge your Avatar<br /> unless you have some form of physical connection to<br /> your phylactery.</b> That form could involve a physical<br /> gateway to virtual contact, as with a computer that<br /> accesses a mainframe, but <b>you still need that gateway<br /> in order to reach a distant phylactery</b>. (Yes, <b>you may use<br /> Correspondence Sphere magick to reach the phylactery,<br /> and you are always counted as being one success away<br /> from your phylactery when you use Correspondence to<br /> reach out to it.</b>)\u200b<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <b>If you\u2019re using your phylactery to cast magick, you need<br /> to be rather obvious about it\u200b</b> </div> </div> </div>So you can not perform magic unless in contact with the Phylactery, BUT the Correspondence sphere can be used to contact it (even if you can not use any other magic???) therefore you could always count as in contact as long as you keep a Correspondence effect with that function (touch my Phylactery) always on... But you need to be blantant that you are using the Phylactery? That you are remotely touching...<br /> <br /> Arent those contradicting statements at some point, because rules as written, you are unable to do magic normally EXCEPT Correspondence to contact the Phylactery, but wthen you use Correspondence to contact your Phylactery, blam you are capable of casting magic as long as you are obvious about it... Which you can not be since it is a remote connection.<br /> <br /> Did i get all that right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-05T23:15:33-07:00","id":1522140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1522033-m20-phylactery?p=1522136#post1522136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is what confuses me, bolded my confusions:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So you can not perform magic unless in contact with the Phylactery, BUT the Correspondence sphere can be used to contact it (even if you can not use any other magic???) therefore you could always count as in contact as long as you keep a Correspondence effect with that function (touch my Phylactery) always on... But you need to be blantant that you are using the Phylactery? That you are remotely touching...<br /> <br /> Arent those contradicting statements at some point, because rules as written, you are unable to do magic normally EXCEPT Correspondence to contact the Phylactery, but wthen you use Correspondence to contact your Phylactery, blam you are capable of casting magic as long as you are obvious about it... Which you can not be since it is a remote connection.<br /> <br /> Did i get all that right?</div> </div> </div> </div>As I read it, it is as simple as this:<br /> <br /> the only magic you can perform without your phylactery is an effect which can get your phylactery back with you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}